IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 1, PRELIMINARY PROVISIONS (ss 1 to 7).
-- ss 1 to 4 (title, commencement, purpose, overview) and s 6 (a pointer to Schedule 1) carry no rule for a person:
-- see the coverage table in NOTES.md. The definitions of s 5(1) are in the glossary module nz-glossary.l4; this
-- module encodes the three that decide something from facts.

§ `Section 5 -- Interpretation`

-- src:75 | secondary legislation means an instrument (whatever it is called) that—
-- src:76 | is made under an Act if the Act (or any other legislation) states that the instrument is secondary legislation; or
-- src:77 | is made under the Royal prerogative in a form and for a purpose set out in Schedule 1A
-- src:78 | Example
-- src:79 | The ABC Act 2018 enables the Governor-General, by Order in Council, either to make exemptions in the Order in Council or to enable the regulator to issue exemption notices. Both the order and notice are made (directly or indirectly) under the ABC Act (see section 21). The ABC Act states that both are secondary legislation. As a result, both the Order in Council and the exemption notice made under that order are secondary legislation under this definition.
-- "secondary legislation means an instrument (whatever it is called) that (a) is made under an Act if the Act (or any other
-- legislation) states that the instrument is secondary legislation; or (b) is made under the Royal prerogative in a form and
-- for a purpose set out in Schedule 1A". Schedule 1A is blank in the deposited text, so (b) takes its form-and-purpose fact as an input.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of secondary legislation (src:75-77) (src:79)
GIVEN instrument IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is secondary legislation` instrument MEANS
        ((instrument's `it is made under an Act, directly or indirectly`) AND (instrument's `the Act, or other legislation, states that it is secondary legislation`))
     OR ((instrument's `it is made under the Royal prerogative`) AND (instrument's `its form and purpose are set out in Schedule 1A`))

-- "legislation means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation"; "instrument includes secondary legislation and
-- any instrument that is not legislation (for example, an administrative document)". A thing that is neither an Act nor secondary
-- legislation is not legislation (the "means" is closed); "instrument" is an "includes" list, so an Act's status as an instrument is silent.
-- src:62 | legislation means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of legislation (src:62)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is legislation` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the whole of an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a part of an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `secondary legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument that is not legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Bill not yet enacted` THEN FALSE

-- src:60 | instrument includes secondary legislation and any instrument that is not legislation (for example, an administrative document)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of instrument (src:60)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is an instrument` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the whole of an Act` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a part of an Act` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `secondary legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument that is not legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Bill not yet enacted` THEN NOTHING

-- The three other s 5(1) definitions that list things. Each says "means", so each is CLOSED: a candidate off the list is not covered, JUST FALSE (ruling C).
DECLARE `Item of information` IS ONE OF
    `the Title of the legislation`
    `the empowering provision`
    `the administering agency`
    `any other information required by regulations made under this Act`
    `the date on which the secondary legislation was made`
    `any other information`

-- src:65 | minimum legislative information means—
-- src:66 | the Title of the legislation; and
-- src:67 | the empowering provision; and
-- src:68 | the administering agency; and
-- src:69 | any other information required by regulations made under this Act
-- "minimum legislative information means the Title of the legislation; and the empowering provision; and the administering agency; and any other information required by regulations made under this Act".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of minimum legislative information (src:65-69)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is minimum legislative information` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `the Title of the legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the empowering provision` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the administering agency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other information required by regulations made under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the date on which the secondary legislation was made` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other information` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for administering agency` IS ONE OF
    `a department`
    `an Office of Parliament`
    `another organisation`
    `a person who is not an organisation`

-- src:47 | administering agency means, in relation to legislation, the department, Office of Parliament, or other organisation that is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation
-- "administering agency means, in relation to legislation, the department, Office of Parliament, or other organisation that is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation". The responsibility condition applies to each.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definition of administering agency (src:47)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for administering agency`
      `it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is the administering agency` candidate `when it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation:` `it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation` MEANS
    IF `it is, or will be, responsible for administering the legislation`
    THEN CONSIDER candidate
         WHEN `a department` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an Office of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another organisation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a person who is not an organisation` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for empowering legislation or provision` IS ONE OF
    `the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument`
    `the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument`
    `the Royal prerogative`
    `other law`

-- src:54 | empowering legislation, in relation to any secondary legislation or instrument, means—
-- src:55 | the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument; or
-- src:56 | the Royal prerogative (for anything done under the Royal prerogative)
-- src:57 | empowering provision, in relation to any secondary legislation or instrument, means—
-- src:58 | the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument; or
-- src:59 | the Royal prerogative (for anything done under the Royal prerogative)
-- "empowering legislation ... means the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument; or the Royal prerogative (for anything done under the Royal prerogative)"; "empowering provision" is the same with "the provision of the empowering legislation".
-- Both say "means", so both are CLOSED. The candidate is checked against each definition separately: the first asks `is empowering legislation`, the second `is the empowering provision`.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(1), definitions of empowering legislation and empowering provision (src:54) (src:55-56) (src:58-59)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for empowering legislation or provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is empowering legislation` candidate MEANS
    CONSIDER candidate
    WHEN `the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the Royal prerogative` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `other law` THEN JUST FALSE

GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for empowering legislation or provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is the empowering provision` candidate MEANS
    CONSIDER candidate
    WHEN `the legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the provision of the empowering legislation that empowers the making of the secondary legislation or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Royal prerogative` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `other law` THEN JUST FALSE

-- "(2) a reference to the maker of any secondary legislation or instrument is, if the Governor-General is empowered to make that
-- legislation or instrument, a reference to the relevant Minister for that secondary legislation or instrument."
DECLARE `Who is the maker` IS ONE OF
    `the person empowered to make it`
    `the relevant Minister`

-- src:81 | In this Act, a reference to the maker of any secondary legislation or instrument is, if the Governor-General is empowered to make that legislation or instrument, a reference to the relevant Minister for that secondary legislation or instrument.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(2) (src:81)
GIVEN `the Governor-General is empowered to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who is the maker`
`who is the maker of the secondary legislation or instrument` `the Governor-General is empowered to make it` MEANS
    IF `the Governor-General is empowered to make it`
    THEN `the relevant Minister`
    ELSE `the person empowered to make it`

-- (3) See also the definitions of terms for all legislation in section 13, which also apply to this Act.
-- src:82 | See also the definitions of terms for all legislation in section 13, which also apply to this Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 5(3) (src:82)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definitions of terms for all legislation in section 13 also apply to this Act` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 6 -- Transitional, savings, and related provisions`

-- src:83 | 6 Transitional, savings, and related provisions
-- src:84 | The transitional, savings, and related provisions set out in Schedule 1 have effect according to their terms.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 6 (src:83) (src:84)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the transitional, savings and related provisions in Schedule 1 have effect according to their terms` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 7 -- Act binds the Crown`

-- src:85 | 7 Act binds the Crown
-- src:86 | This Act binds the Crown.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 7 (src:85-86)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this Act binds the Crown` MEANS TRUE
